TIP:  The intro is a three-note pick and a strum of (D) (notes may or may not transpose).  Untransposed, start by forming (D/A) with your pinky on the 4th string/4th fret <f>.  Now lift off the index finger from the 3rd string/2nd fret so the 3rd string is now open.  Okay, now pick the covered 4th string <f#>, pick the open 3rd string <g> while lifting off the pinky, replace the index finger (chord (D) and strum the 3 treble strings, and finish with a good thump of the open 4th string <d>.
 

